{"name":"Healing Aloe","hex":"#b9cab3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"healing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process where the cells in the body regenerate and repair themselves.","An act of healing, as by a faith healer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of heal"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healing"},{"term":"aloe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The resins of the tree Aquilaria malaccensis (syn. Aquilaria agallocha), known for their fragrant aroma, produced after infection by the fungus Phialophora parasitica.","Any plant of the large and variable genus Aloe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Healing","blocks":[{"text":"Regarding physical trauma or disease suffered by an organism, healing involves the repairing of damaged tissue(s), organs and the biological system as a whole and resumption of (normal) functioning. Medicine includes the process by which the cells in the body regenerate and repair to reduce the size of a damaged or necrotic area and replace it with new living tissue. The replacement can happen in two ways: by regeneration in which the necrotic cells are replaced by new cells that form \"like\" tissue as was originally there; or by repair in which injured tissue is replaced with scar tissue. Most organs will heal using a mixture of both mechanisms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/417_Tissue_Repair.jpg/330px-417_Tissue_Repair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healing","wikidata":"Q1581290"},{"title":"Aloe","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe is a genus containing 594 species of flowering succulent plants. The most widely known species is Aloe vera, or \"true aloe\", which is cultivated as a source for topical uses and dietary supplements. Other species, such as Aloe ferox, are also cultivated or harvested from the wild for similar applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg/330px-Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe","wikidata":"Q127134"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/1280px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wounded patients at the Red Cross Hospital in Tampere, Finland during the 1918 Finnish Civil War","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_(26901645371).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Split_Aloe.jpg/500px-Split_Aloe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Split_Aloe.jpg/1280px-Split_Aloe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Split_Aloe.jpg/500px-Split_Aloe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum